le queries do not provide the individual event timestamps needed to establish a temporally ordered chain with gaps \u2264600. The direct edge query shows no direct interactions between 1885 and 1460 in the window (step_02) and the windowed counts show some activity but only coarse temporal bins (step_05). K-hop neighbourhoods show static connectivity possibilities when time is ignored (steps_01 and _03) and node degrees show both nodes were active (step_04), but none of the returned results provide the exact event times or ordered event sequence required to demonstrate a time-respecting cascade, so the evidence is insufficient.\"\n}", "total_input_tokens": 24791, "total_output_tokens": 2826, "total_tokens": 27617, "total_latency_ms": 41381, "llm_calls": 6, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}